 "findings": {
  "unlock": "Against the untuned base under the same prompts and decoders, the E2b adapter raises Cityscapes mIoU 21.5 → 34.2 and RefCOCOg cIoU 37.6 → 49.8; the cube-edge depth run C1 raises NYU δ1 0.072 → 0.348.",
  "quarter": "E2b (¼ of the vision rows) at 10k: Cityscapes 34.2 vs 33.1, RefCOCOg 49.8 vs 33.7, NYU δ1 0.134 vs 0.043 for E1 at the same step.",
  "longer": "RefCOCOg cIoU of the six-task run by step: 49.7 at 5k, 33.7 at 10k, 40.9 at 15k, 42.3 at 30k; Cityscapes stays between 27.2 and 33.1.",
  "noise": "Same checkpoint, inference seed 42 vs 43: ≤ 1.0 points on 2D, ≤ 0.014 δ1 on depth; re-evaluating the same E2b checkpoint moved Cityscapes by 1.1. Two training seeds at vision_ratio 0.2 differ by 14.2 RefCOCOg points — most ablation gaps below that are not separable from seed noise.",
  "cube": "Fixing the depth target to the cube-edge colormap (C1) gives the best metric depth so far: NYU δ1 0.140 → 0.348, AbsRel 1.455 → 0.585; T2 with five colormaps reaches 0.179.",
  "seg": "No task mix moved Cityscapes above the parent's 35.3; the segmentation-only mix T3 is the lowest at 26.4.",
  "full": "Full fine-tuning at lr 3e-5 cut RefCOCOg cIoU 49.9 → 30.3 and moved generation away from the base (FID-proxy 1.63 → 5.41); continuing the LoRA kept it at 1.68.",
  "fresh": "A fresh rsLoRA trained for 10k steps on the untuned base gave the highest 2D scores of any run: Cityscapes 36.9, RefCOCOg 52.9, ReasonSeg 36.6 — but metric depth stayed near the base (NYU δ1 0.080)."
 },
